A||N||4||Daleford||Ground Control coil-over kits -Good or bad idea? ||||1||
Z||000000||Daleford||12-04-2001||03:30 PM||||Considering buying a set of these for the rear of a 86 Fiero. Anybody had good/bad experiences with them?<BR>Thanking you in advance.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||VISCERAL||12-04-2001||04:58 PM||||That all depends how you do your setup they give you an 8" eibach spring and a 4" aluminum threaded sleeve. These will rest on your strut perch. Mine likes to bottom out on nasty holes. The proper way is to get a 10" eibach from them and a 8" sleeve and cut off your spring perch to let it rest on the bottom of your strut. You will get more adjustable range this way. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||12-04-2001||05:06 PM||||try inverting the bump-stop plate on your coil over assy. This will gain you 1 1/2" of suspension travel before hitting the bump stop. There will be minimum grinding around the curcumference of the bumpstop area for it to pass through the cars' chassis and to be mounted. With this you can retain the 8" spring included with the kit. We also do this procedure inhouse for those in which we install lowering springs, it will net you the same effect<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000003||Daleford||12-04-2001||08:16 PM||||I just found another coil-over kit company. Wondering if anyone ever used their coils or if they even make kits for Fieros.<BR>It is Toucan Industries and their spring kits use the name Ractive.  Any info anybody?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||12-04-2001||11:44 PM||||Held Motorsports is having a group buy this month, there is a thread in General Chat for it.  They have top-of-the line products, and offer a VERY wide array of spring choices with the coilovers.  They are very helpful, and specialize in Fiero suspension and braking components, check them out!  <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.heldmotorsports.com/</A> <P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
